import LeanBridge.ForMathlib.NumberTheory.ModularForms.Newform.Dimension
import LeanBridge.ForMathlib.NumberTheory.ModularForms.Newform.TraceBoundExists
import Mathlib.RingTheory.TensorProduct.Basic
import TauCeti.NumberTheory.ModularForms.Newforms.BadPrime.Stability
import TauCeti.NumberTheory.ModularForms.Newforms.Hecke.Rational

/-!
# Galois conjugates of newforms and the rational Hecke algebra

For an automorphism `σ` of `ℂ` and a newform `f = ∑ aₙ qⁿ` of level `N` and weight `k`, the Galois
conjugate `σ(f) = ∑ σ(aₙ) qⁿ` is again a newform of level `N` and weight `k` (Shimura). This is
LeanBridge issue #38, on which the Galois orbits of newforms (LMFDB `cmf.galois_orbit`), their
embeddings (LMFDB `cmf.embedding`), the decompositions of the spaces of newforms (LMFDB
`cmf.decomposition.new.gamma0chi`, `cmf.decomposition.new.gamma1`, `cmf.newspaces`) and the trace
bound (LMFDB `cmf.trace_bound`) rest. This file reduces it to a statement about the Hecke algebra
alone, and proves the reduction.

Let `T_ℚ` be the `ℚ`-subalgebra of `End_ℂ(S_k(Γ₁(N))ⁿᵉʷ)` generated by the Hecke operators `T_p` at
all primes `p` (the operators `U_p` at `p ∣ N`) and the diamond operators. Its complex span is
Tau Ceti's complex newspace Hecke algebra `T_ℂ`, the algebra of the operators that are diagonal in
the basis of newforms, whose characters are those of the newforms
(`TauCeti.Newform.heckeTDiamondCuspNewCharacterEquiv`). The hypothesis is that `T_ℚ` is a
`ℚ`-form of `T_ℂ`: the natural map `ℂ ⊗_ℚ T_ℚ → End_ℂ(S_k(Γ₁(N))ⁿᵉʷ)` is injective, i.e. operators
of `T_ℚ` that are linearly independent over `ℚ` stay linearly independent over `ℂ`. It holds as
soon as `S_k(Γ₁(N))` has a `ℚ`-structure stable under the Hecke and diamond operators, such as the
forms with rational Fourier coefficients (Shimura, *Introduction to the arithmetic theory of
automorphic functions*, Theorem 3.52), or by the Eichler–Shimura isomorphism; neither is available
in Mathlib or Tau Ceti, which prove only that the integral Hecke algebra is a finite `ℤ`-module
(`TauCeti.heckeTCuspAlgebra_finite`, through the injective period map into modular symbols), and
that does not give it. So the hypothesis is not proved here. It is also necessary: in weight at
least two it is equivalent to the theorem (`HeckeRing.GL2.Newform.hasRationalHeckeForm_iff`), so
that it is exactly the missing input.

Given the hypothesis, the proof is algebra: the character `σ ∘ λ_f` of `T_ℚ` extends to a
character of `ℂ ⊗_ℚ T_ℚ ≅ T_ℂ`, which is the character `λ_g` of a newform `g`; then
`a_p(g) = σ(a_p(f))` at every prime `p`, the nebentypus of `g` is `σ ∘ χ`, and the Hecke recurrence
gives `aₙ(g) = σ(aₙ(f))` for all `n`.

Without the hypothesis, the rational Hecke algebra already cuts the newspace into the pieces of the
LMFDB decomposition (LMFDB `cmf.decomposition.new.gamma0chi`, `cmf.newspaces`): in weight at least
two, two newforms are Galois conjugate exactly when their characters on `T_ℚ` have the same kernel,
and the vectors killed by that kernel form the span of their Galois orbit. What is missing for the
LMFDB statements is that each piece has dimension `[ℚ(f) : ℚ]`, i.e. that all the Galois conjugates
of `f` are newforms.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.heckeTCuspNewEndOfPrime`: the Hecke operator `T_p` on the newspace, at any prime `p`.
* `TauCeti.heckeCuspNewRationalAlgebra`: the rational Hecke algebra `T_ℚ` of the newspace
  (LMFDB `cmf.decomposition.new.gamma0chi`).
* `TauCeti.heckeCuspNewComplexify`: the natural map `ℂ ⊗_ℚ T_ℚ → End_ℂ(S_k(Γ₁(N))ⁿᵉʷ)`.
* `TauCeti.HasRationalHeckeForm`: the natural map `ℂ ⊗_ℚ T_ℚ → End_ℂ(S_k(Γ₁(N))ⁿᵉʷ)` is injective.
* `TauCeti.heckeCuspNewRationalAlgebraToComplex`: the inclusion of `T_ℚ` into the complex newspace
  Hecke algebra.
* `TauCeti.heckeCuspNewPiece`: the piece of the newspace cut out by an ideal of `T_ℚ`
  (LMFDB `cmf.decomposition.new.gamma0chi`).
* `HeckeRing.GL2.Newform.heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter`: the character of a newform on `T_ℚ`.
* `HeckeRing.GL2.Newform.galoisConj`: the Galois conjugate `σ(f)` as a newform, if `T_ℚ` is a
  `ℚ`-form (LMFDB `cmf.newspaces`).

## Main results

* `TauCeti.range_heckeCuspNewComplexify`: the complex span of `T_ℚ` is the complex newspace Hecke
  algebra.
* `HeckeRing.GL2.Newform.isGaloisConjugate_iff_ker_heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter_le`,
  `HeckeRing.GL2.Newform.isGaloisConjugate_iff_ker_heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter_eq`: in weight at
  least two, the Galois orbits of newforms are the fibres of the kernels of their characters on
  `T_ℚ`.
* `HeckeRing.GL2.Newform.map_heckeCuspNewPiece_ker`: in weight at least two, the piece of the
  newspace cut out by the kernel of the character of a newform `f` on `T_ℚ` is the span of the
  Galois orbit of `f`.
* `HeckeRing.GL2.Newform.exists_isGaloisConjugateBy_of_hasRationalHeckeForm`: if `T_ℚ` is a
  `ℚ`-form, every Galois conjugate `σ(f)` of a newform `f` is a newform (LeanBridge issue #38).
* `HeckeRing.GL2.Newform.hasRationalHeckeForm_iff`: in weight at least two, `T_ℚ` is a `ℚ`-form
  exactly when every Galois conjugate of a newform is a newform.
* `HeckeRing.GL2.Newform.galoisConj_mul`, `HeckeRing.GL2.Newform.exists_galoisConj_eq_iff`: then
  the Galois group acts on the newforms, with the Galois orbits as orbits (LMFDB `cmf.newspaces`).
* `HeckeRing.GL2.Newform.exists_isEmbedding_of_hasRationalHeckeForm`: then every embedding `ι` of
  the coefficient field gives a newform `ι(f)` (LMFDB `cmf.embedding`).
* `HeckeRing.GL2.Newform.dimension_eq_finrank_of_hasRationalHeckeForm`: then in weight at least
  two the newform subspace of `f` has dimension `[ℚ(f) : ℚ]`
  (LMFDB `cmf.decomposition.new.gamma0chi`).
* `HeckeRing.GL2.Newform.image_galoisConj_setOf_χ_eq`,
  `HeckeRing.GL2.Newform.finrank_cuspFormsNew_inf_cuspFormCharSpace_comp_of_hasRationalHeckeForm`:
  then `σ` maps the newforms of `S_k^{new}(N, χ)` onto those of `S_k^{new}(N, σ ∘ χ)`, and the two
  spaces have the same dimension (LMFDB `cmf.decomposition.new.gamma1`).
* `HeckeRing.GL2.Newform.exists_tracesDistinguishNewforms_of_hasRationalHeckeForm`: then in weight
  at least two the trace bound exists (LMFDB `cmf.trace_bound`).
-/

open UpperHalfPlane HeckeRing GL2 Algebra TensorProduct TauCeti Module

namespace TauCeti

variable (N : ℕ) [NeZero N] (k : ℤ) {p : ℕ} (hp : p.Prime)

/-- The restriction to the new subspace of the Hecke operator `T_p` at a prime `p`, which is `U_p`
when `p ∣ N`. -/
noncomputable def heckeTCuspNewEndOfPrime : Module.End ℂ (cuspFormsNew N k) :=
  (heckeTCuspNat k p (_hn := ⟨hp.ne_zero⟩)).restrict fun _ ↦ heckeTCuspNat_mem_cuspFormsNew hp

/-- The **rational Hecke algebra** `T_ℚ` of the newspace `S_k(Γ₁(N))ⁿᵉʷ`
(LMFDB `cmf.decomposition.new.gamma0chi`): the `ℚ`-subalgebra of its complex endomorphisms
generated by the Hecke operators `T_p` at all primes `p` and the diamond operators. Tau Ceti's
`TauCeti.heckeTDiamondCuspNewRationalAlgebra` is the subalgebra generated by the `T_p` at the
primes `p ∤ N` and the diamond operators. -/
noncomputable def heckeCuspNewRationalAlgebra : Subalgebra ℚ (Module.End ℂ (cuspFormsNew N k)) :=
  adjoin ℚ (Set.range (fun p : {p : ℕ // p.Prime} ↦ heckeTCuspNewEndOfPrime N k p.2) ∪
    Set.range (diamondOpCuspNewEnd N k))

/-- The natural map `ℂ ⊗_ℚ T_ℚ → End_ℂ(S_k(Γ₁(N))ⁿᵉʷ)`, `c ⊗ t ↦ c • t`. -/
noncomputable def heckeCuspNewComplexify :
    ℂ ⊗[ℚ] heckeCuspNewRationalAlgebra N k →ₐ[ℂ] Module.End ℂ (cuspFormsNew N k) :=
  lift (ofId ℂ _) (heckeCuspNewRationalAlgebra N k).val fun _ _ ↦ commute_algebraMap_left _ _

/-- The rational Hecke algebra `T_ℚ` of the newspace `S_k(Γ₁(N))ⁿᵉʷ` **is a `ℚ`-form** of its
complex span: the natural map `ℂ ⊗_ℚ T_ℚ → End_ℂ(S_k(Γ₁(N))ⁿᵉʷ)` is injective, i.e. elements of
`T_ℚ` that are linearly independent over `ℚ` are linearly independent over `ℂ`. This is a theorem
(it follows from the existence of a `ℚ`-structure on `S_k(Γ₁(N))` stable under the Hecke and
diamond operators), which is not proved here; it is the hypothesis under which Galois conjugates
of newforms are shown to be newforms, and in weight at least two it is equivalent to that
(`HeckeRing.GL2.Newform.hasRationalHeckeForm_iff`). -/
def HasRationalHeckeForm : Prop :=
  Function.Injective (heckeCuspNewComplexify N k)

variable {N k}

lemma heckeTCuspNewEndOfPrime_mem :
    heckeTCuspNewEndOfPrime N k hp ∈ heckeCuspNewRationalAlgebra N k :=
  subset_adjoin <| Set.mem_union_left _ ⟨⟨p, hp⟩, rfl⟩

lemma diamondOpCuspNewEnd_mem_heckeCuspNewRationalAlgebra (u : (ZMod N)ˣ) :
    diamondOpCuspNewEnd N k u ∈ heckeCuspNewRationalAlgebra N k :=
  subset_adjoin <| Set.mem_union_right _ ⟨u, rfl⟩

lemma heckeTCuspNewEndOfPrime_basis (f : Newform N k) :
    heckeTCuspNewEndOfPrime N k hp (Newform.basis N k f) =
      (qExpansion 1 f.toCuspForm).coeff p • Newform.basis N k f :=
  Subtype.ext <| by
    simpa [heckeTCuspNewEndOfPrime] using f.heckeTCuspNat_eq_qExpansion_coeff_smul hp

lemma mem_heckeTDiamondCuspNewAlgebra_of_forall_basis {T : Module.End ℂ (cuspFormsNew N k)}
    (c : Newform N k → ℂ) (hT : ∀ f, T (Newform.basis N k f) = c f • Newform.basis N k f) :
    T ∈ heckeTDiamondCuspNewAlgebra N k := by
  have h : T = (Newform.heckeTDiamondCuspNewAlgebraEquiv.symm c).1 := by
    refine (Newform.basis N k).ext fun f ↦ ?_
    rw [hT, Newform.apply_basis_eq_heckeTDiamondCuspNewCharacter_smul,
      ← Newform.heckeTDiamondCuspNewAlgebraEquiv_apply, AlgEquiv.apply_symm_apply]
  exact h ▸ (Newform.heckeTDiamondCuspNewAlgebraEquiv.symm c).2

lemma heckeCuspNewRationalAlgebra_le :
    heckeCuspNewRationalAlgebra N k ≤ (heckeTDiamondCuspNewAlgebra N k).restrictScalars ℚ := by
  refine adjoin_le (Set.union_subset ?_ ?_)
  · rintro _ ⟨p, rfl⟩
    exact mem_heckeTDiamondCuspNewAlgebra_of_forall_basis _ fun f ↦
      heckeTCuspNewEndOfPrime_basis p.2 f
  · rintro _ ⟨u, rfl⟩
    exact diamondOpCuspNewEnd_mem_heckeTDiamondCuspNewAlgebra N k u

variable (N k) in
/-- The inclusion of the rational Hecke algebra of the newspace into the complex newspace Hecke
algebra. -/
noncomputable def heckeCuspNewRationalAlgebraToComplex :
    heckeCuspNewRationalAlgebra N k →ₐ[ℚ] heckeTDiamondCuspNewAlgebra N k :=
  (heckeCuspNewRationalAlgebra N k).val.codRestrict _ fun t ↦ heckeCuspNewRationalAlgebra_le t.2

lemma heckeCuspNewComplexify_tmul (c : ℂ) (t : heckeCuspNewRationalAlgebra N k) :
    heckeCuspNewComplexify N k (c ⊗ₜ t) = c • (t : Module.End ℂ (cuspFormsNew N k)) :=
  (lift_tmul _ _ _ c t).trans (smul_def c _).symm

lemma heckeCuspNewComplexify_mem (x : ℂ ⊗[ℚ] heckeCuspNewRationalAlgebra N k) :
    heckeCuspNewComplexify N k x ∈ heckeTDiamondCuspNewAlgebra N k := by
  induction x using TensorProduct.inductionOn with
  | tmul c t =>
    rw [heckeCuspNewComplexify_tmul]
    exact (heckeTDiamondCuspNewAlgebra N k).smul_mem (heckeCuspNewRationalAlgebra_le t.2) c
  | add x y hx hy => simpa using add_mem hx hy

/-- **The complex span of the rational Hecke algebra of the newspace is the complex newspace Hecke
algebra**: the image of `ℂ ⊗_ℚ T_ℚ` is the algebra generated over `ℂ` by the `T_p` at the primes
`p ∤ N` and the diamond operators. In particular the operators `U_p` at the primes `p ∣ N` lie in
it, as they are diagonal in the basis of newforms. -/
lemma range_heckeCuspNewComplexify :
    (heckeCuspNewComplexify N k).range = heckeTDiamondCuspNewAlgebra N k := by
  refine le_antisymm (fun _ hx ↦ ?_) ((heckeTDiamondCuspNewAlgebra_le_iff N k _).mpr
    ⟨fun p hp _ ↦ (heckeCuspNewComplexify N k).mem_range.mpr
      ⟨1 ⊗ₜ ⟨_, heckeTCuspNewEndOfPrime_mem hp⟩, ?_⟩,
      fun u ↦ (heckeCuspNewComplexify N k).mem_range.mpr
        ⟨1 ⊗ₜ ⟨_, diamondOpCuspNewEnd_mem_heckeCuspNewRationalAlgebra u⟩, ?_⟩⟩)
  · rcases (heckeCuspNewComplexify N k).mem_range.mp hx with ⟨x, rfl⟩
    exact heckeCuspNewComplexify_mem x
  · rw [heckeCuspNewComplexify_tmul, one_smul]
    rfl
  · rw [heckeCuspNewComplexify_tmul, one_smul]

variable (N k) in
/-- The **piece** of the newspace `S_k(Γ₁(N))ⁿᵉʷ` cut out by an ideal `I` of its rational Hecke
algebra `T_ℚ` (LMFDB `cmf.decomposition.new.gamma0chi`): the vectors killed by every operator of
`I`. For the kernel of the character of `T_ℚ` on a newform `f`, it is the span of the Galois orbit
of `f` (`HeckeRing.GL2.Newform.map_heckeCuspNewPiece_ker`): the newspace breaks up under the Hecke
algebra into these pieces. -/
noncomputable def heckeCuspNewPiece (I : Ideal (heckeCuspNewRationalAlgebra N k)) :
    Submodule ℂ (cuspFormsNew N k) :=
  ⨅ t ∈ I, LinearMap.ker (t : Module.End ℂ (cuspFormsNew N k))

end TauCeti

namespace HeckeRing.GL2.Newform

variable {N : ℕ} [NeZero N] {k : ℤ} {f g : Newform N k} {σ τ : Gal(ℂ/ℚ)}
  (t : heckeCuspNewRationalAlgebra N k) (χ : (ZMod N)ˣ →* ℂˣ)

variable (f) in
/-- The character of a newform `f` on the rational Hecke algebra `T_ℚ` of the newspace: the
eigenvalue of an operator of `T_ℚ` on `f`. It sends `T_p` to `a_p(f)` and the diamond operator
`⟨u⟩` to `χ(u)`. -/
noncomputable def heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter : heckeCuspNewRationalAlgebra N k →ₐ[ℚ] ℂ :=
  ((Newform.heckeTDiamondCuspNewCharacter f).restrictScalars ℚ).comp
    (heckeCuspNewRationalAlgebraToComplex N k)

lemma heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter_apply : f.heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter t =
    Newform.heckeTDiamondCuspNewCharacter f ⟨t, heckeCuspNewRationalAlgebra_le t.2⟩ :=
  rfl

lemma apply_basis_eq_heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter_smul :
    (t : Module.End ℂ (cuspFormsNew N k)) (basis N k f) =
      f.heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter t • basis N k f :=
  Newform.apply_basis_eq_heckeTDiamondCuspNewCharacter_smul f ⟨t, _⟩

lemma heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter_heckeTCuspNewEndOfPrime {p : ℕ} (hp : p.Prime) :
    f.heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter ⟨_, heckeTCuspNewEndOfPrime_mem hp⟩ =
      (qExpansion 1 f.toCuspForm).coeff p :=
  smul_left_injective ℂ ((basis N k).ne_zero f) <|
    (apply_basis_eq_heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter_smul _).symm.trans
      (heckeTCuspNewEndOfPrime_basis hp f)

lemma heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter_diamondOpCuspNewEnd (u : (ZMod N)ˣ) :
    f.heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter ⟨_, diamondOpCuspNewEnd_mem_heckeCuspNewRationalAlgebra u⟩ =
      f.χ u :=
  smul_left_injective ℂ ((basis N k).ne_zero f) <|
    (apply_basis_eq_heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter_smul _).symm.trans (diamondOpCuspNewEnd_basis u f)

lemma dirichletLift_apply_eq_of_forall_χ (hχ : ∀ u : (ZMod N)ˣ, (g.χ u : ℂ) = σ (f.χ u))
    (x : ZMod N) : g.dirichletLift x = σ (f.dirichletLift x) := by
  by_cases hx : IsUnit x
  · rcases hx with ⟨u, rfl⟩
    rw [dirichletLift_def, dirichletLift_def, MulChar.ofUnitHom_coe, MulChar.ofUnitHom_coe, hχ]
  · rw [MulChar.map_nonunit _ hx, MulChar.map_nonunit _ hx, map_zero]

lemma qExpansion_coeff_eq_of_forall_prime
    (hp : ∀ p : ℕ, p.Prime →
      (qExpansion 1 g.toCuspForm).coeff p = σ ((qExpansion 1 f.toCuspForm).coeff p))
    (hχ : ∀ u : (ZMod N)ˣ, (g.χ u : ℂ) = σ (f.χ u)) (n : ℕ) :
    (qExpansion 1 g.toCuspForm).coeff n = σ ((qExpansion 1 f.toCuspForm).coeff n) := by
  have hχ' (p : ℕ) : (MulChar.ofUnitHom g.χ : DirichletCharacter ℂ N) p =
      σ ((MulChar.ofUnitHom f.χ : DirichletCharacter ℂ N) p) :=
    dirichletLift_apply_eq_of_forall_χ hχ p
  induction n using Nat.recOnPrimeCoprime with
  | zero =>
    rw [CuspFormClass.qExpansion_coeff_zero g.toCuspForm one_pos
      (one_mem_strictPeriods_Gamma1_map N), CuspFormClass.qExpansion_coeff_zero f.toCuspForm
      one_pos (one_mem_strictPeriods_Gamma1_map N), map_zero]
  | prime_pow p r hpp =>
    induction r using Nat.twoStepInduction with
    | zero => simp
    | one => simpa using hp p hpp
    | more r ih₁ ih₂ =>
      rw [← g.toEigenform_toCuspForm, ← f.toEigenform_toCuspForm,
        g.toEigenform.qExpansion_coeff_prime_pow_add_two g.toEigenform_qExpansion_coeff_one hpp r,
        f.toEigenform.qExpansion_coeff_prime_pow_add_two f.toEigenform_qExpansion_coeff_one hpp r,
        toEigenform_toCuspForm, toEigenform_toCuspForm, toEigenform_χ, toEigenform_χ, ih₁, ih₂,
        hp p hpp, hχ' p]
      simp
  | coprime a b _ _ hab iha ihb =>
    rw [← g.toEigenform_toCuspForm, ← f.toEigenform_toCuspForm,
      g.toEigenform.qExpansion_coeff_mul g.toEigenform_qExpansion_coeff_one hab,
      f.toEigenform.qExpansion_coeff_mul f.toEigenform_qExpansion_coeff_one hab,
      toEigenform_toCuspForm, toEigenform_toCuspForm, iha, ihb, map_mul]

lemma IsGaloisConjugateBy.heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter_eq (hfg : f.IsGaloisConjugateBy σ g) :
    g.heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter = (σ : ℂ →ₐ[ℚ] ℂ).comp f.heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter :=
  AlgHom.ext_of_eq_adjoin (S := heckeCuspNewRationalAlgebra N k) rfl fun x hx ↦ by
    rcases hx with ⟨p, rfl⟩ | ⟨u, rfl⟩
    · rw [AlgHom.comp_apply, heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter_heckeTCuspNewEndOfPrime,
        heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter_heckeTCuspNewEndOfPrime, hfg.coeff]
      rfl
    · rw [AlgHom.comp_apply, heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter_diamondOpCuspNewEnd,
        heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter_diamondOpCuspNewEnd, hfg.χ_apply]
      rfl

lemma isGaloisConjugateBy_of_heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter_eq
    (h : ∀ t, g.heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter t = σ (f.heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter t)) :
    f.IsGaloisConjugateBy σ g := by
  refine isGaloisConjugateBy_iff.mpr <| qExpansion_coeff_eq_of_forall_prime (fun p hp ↦ ?_)
    fun u ↦ ?_
  · rw [← heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter_heckeTCuspNewEndOfPrime hp,
      ← heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter_heckeTCuspNewEndOfPrime hp, h]
  · rw [← heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter_diamondOpCuspNewEnd,
      ← heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter_diamondOpCuspNewEnd, h]

lemma heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter_mem_coefficientField :
    f.heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter t ∈ CoefficientField f := by
  have key (x : Module.End ℂ (cuspFormsNew N k)) (hx : x ∈ heckeCuspNewRationalAlgebra N k) :
      ∀ hx' : x ∈ heckeCuspNewRationalAlgebra N k,
        f.heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter ⟨x, hx'⟩ ∈ CoefficientField f := by
    induction hx using Algebra.adjoin_induction with
    | mem x hx =>
      rcases hx with ⟨p, rfl⟩ | ⟨u, rfl⟩
      · intro hx'
        rw [heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter_heckeTCuspNewEndOfPrime]
        exact coeff_mem_CoefficientField f ⟨p, p.2.pos⟩
      · intro hx'
        rw [heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter_diamondOpCuspNewEnd]
        exact char_mem_CoefficientField f u
    | algebraMap r =>
      intro hx'
      have e : (⟨_, hx'⟩ : heckeCuspNewRationalAlgebra N k) = algebraMap ℚ _ r := rfl
      rw [e, AlgHom.commutes]
      exact IntermediateField.algebraMap_mem _ r
    | add x y hx hy ihx ihy =>
      intro hx'
      have e : (⟨_, hx'⟩ : heckeCuspNewRationalAlgebra N k) = ⟨x, hx⟩ + ⟨y, hy⟩ := rfl
      rw [e, map_add]
      exact add_mem (ihx hx) (ihy hy)
    | mul x y hx hy ihx ihy =>
      intro hx'
      have e : (⟨_, hx'⟩ : heckeCuspNewRationalAlgebra N k) = ⟨x, hx⟩ * ⟨y, hy⟩ := rfl
      rw [e, map_mul]
      exact mul_mem (ihx hx) (ihy hy)
  exact key t t.2 t.2

/-- **The Galois orbits of newforms are cut out by the rational Hecke algebra**: in weight at least
two, a newform `g` is Galois conjugate to the newform `f` exactly when its character `λ_g` on the
rational Hecke algebra `T_ℚ` of the newspace vanishes on the kernel of the character `λ_f` of `f`.
This holds without knowing that all Galois conjugates of newforms are newforms. If `λ_g` vanishes on
the kernel of `λ_f`, then `λ_g = σ ∘ λ_f` for an automorphism `σ` of `ℂ` extending the induced
embedding of the number field `λ_f(T_ℚ)`, and then `g = σ(f)` by the Hecke recurrence. -/
lemma isGaloisConjugate_iff_ker_heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter_le (hk : 2 ≤ k) :
    f.IsGaloisConjugate g ↔ RingHom.ker f.heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter ≤
      RingHom.ker g.heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter := by
  refine ⟨fun ⟨σ, hσ⟩ t ht ↦ ?_, fun h ↦ ?_⟩
  · rw [RingHom.mem_ker, hσ.heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter_eq, AlgHom.comp_apply,
      RingHom.mem_ker.mp ht, map_zero]
  have : NumberField (CoefficientField f) := numberField_CoefficientField f hk
  let R : Subalgebra ℚ (ℂ × ℂ) :=
    (f.heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter.prod g.heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter).range
  let pr : R →ₐ[ℚ] ℂ := (AlgHom.fst ℚ ℂ ℂ).comp R.val
  have hpr : Function.Injective pr := by
    rintro ⟨_, t, rfl⟩ ⟨_, t', rfl⟩ htt'
    have h₁ : f.heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter t = f.heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter t' := htt'
    have hker : t - t' ∈ RingHom.ker g.heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter :=
      h <| RingHom.mem_ker.mpr ((map_sub _ t t').trans (sub_eq_zero.mpr h₁))
    exact Subtype.ext <| Prod.ext h₁ <| sub_eq_zero.mp <|
      (map_sub g.heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter t t').symm.trans (RingHom.mem_ker.mp hker)
  have hsub : (pr.range : Set ℂ) ⊆ CoefficientField f := by
    rintro _ ⟨⟨_, t, rfl⟩, rfl⟩
    exact heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter_mem_coefficientField t
  let L : IntermediateField ℚ ℂ := pr.range.toIntermediateField fun x hx ↦
    pr.range.inv_mem_of_algebraic (x := ⟨x, hx⟩) <| (IntermediateField.isAlgebraic_iff
      (x := (⟨x, hsub hx⟩ : CoefficientField f))).mp (IsAlgebraic.isAlgebraic _)
  have : Countable (CoefficientField f : Set ℂ) := inferInstanceAs (Countable (CoefficientField f))
  have : Countable L := (Set.inclusion_injective hsub).countable
  let ι : L →ₐ[ℚ] ℂ :=
    ((AlgHom.snd ℚ ℂ ℂ).comp R.val).comp (AlgEquiv.ofInjective pr hpr).symm.toAlgHom
  rcases IntermediateField.exists_algEquiv_apply_eq_of_countable ι with ⟨σ, hσ⟩
  have key (t : heckeCuspNewRationalAlgebra N k) :
      g.heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter t = σ (f.heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter t) := by
    have he : (AlgEquiv.ofInjective pr hpr).symm
        ⟨f.heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter t, ⟨_, t, rfl⟩, rfl⟩ = ⟨_, t, rfl⟩ :=
      (AlgEquiv.symm_apply_eq _).mpr <|
        Subtype.ext (AlgEquiv.ofInjective_apply pr hpr ⟨_, t, rfl⟩).symm
    exact ((hσ ⟨_, ⟨_, t, rfl⟩, rfl⟩).trans (congrArg (fun r : R ↦ (r : ℂ × ℂ).2) he)).symm
  exact ⟨σ, isGaloisConjugateBy_of_heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter_eq key⟩

/-- **The Galois orbits of newforms are the fibres of the rational Hecke characters**: in weight at
least two, two newforms are Galois conjugate exactly when their characters on the rational Hecke
algebra `T_ℚ` of the newspace have the same kernel. The newforms whose characters have a given
kernel thus form a Galois orbit, and span its piece of the newspace (LMFDB
`cmf.decomposition.new.gamma0chi`, `cmf.newspaces`). -/
lemma isGaloisConjugate_iff_ker_heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter_eq (hk : 2 ≤ k) :
    f.IsGaloisConjugate g ↔ RingHom.ker f.heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter =
      RingHom.ker g.heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter :=
  ⟨fun h ↦ ((isGaloisConjugate_iff_ker_heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter_le hk).mp h).antisymm
    ((isGaloisConjugate_iff_ker_heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter_le hk).mp h.symm),
    fun h ↦ (isGaloisConjugate_iff_ker_heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter_le hk).mpr h.le⟩

lemma basis_repr_apply_heckeCuspNewRationalAlgebra (v : cuspFormsNew N k) :
    (basis N k).repr ((t : Module.End ℂ (cuspFormsNew N k)) v) g =
      g.heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter t * (basis N k).repr v g := by
  have h : ((basis N k).coord g).comp (t : Module.End ℂ (cuspFormsNew N k)) =
      g.heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter t • (basis N k).coord g := by
    refine (basis N k).ext fun h ↦ ?_
    rw [LinearMap.comp_apply, apply_basis_eq_heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter_smul, map_smul,
      LinearMap.smul_apply, (basis N k).coord_apply, (basis N k).repr_self]
    rcases eq_or_ne h g with rfl | hne
    · rfl
    · simp [hne]
  exact LinearMap.congr_fun h v

variable (f) in
/-- **The newspace breaks up under the rational Hecke algebra into the spans of the Galois
orbits**: in weight at least two, the piece of the newspace cut out by the kernel of the character
of the rational Hecke algebra `T_ℚ` on a newform `f` is the newform subspace of `f`, the span of
its Galois orbit (LMFDB `cmf.decomposition.new.gamma0chi`, `cmf.newspaces`). -/
lemma map_heckeCuspNewPiece_ker (hk : 2 ≤ k) :
    (heckeCuspNewPiece N k (RingHom.ker f.heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter)).map
      (cuspFormsNew N k).subtype = f.newformSubspace := by
  classical
  have : Fintype (Newform N k) := Fintype.ofFinite _
  refine le_antisymm ?_ (Submodule.span_le.mpr ?_)
  · rintro _ ⟨v, hv, rfl⟩
    rw [← (basis N k).sum_repr v, map_sum]
    refine Submodule.sum_mem _ fun g _ ↦ ?_
    rw [map_smul, Submodule.subtype_apply, coe_basis_apply]
    by_cases hg : (basis N k).repr v g = 0
    · rw [hg, zero_smul]
      exact zero_mem _
    refine Submodule.smul_mem _ _ <| toCuspForm_mem_newformSubspace <|
      (isGaloisConjugate_iff_ker_heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter_le hk).mpr fun t ht ↦ ?_
    have h₀ : (t : Module.End ℂ (cuspFormsNew N k)) v = 0 :=
      (Submodule.mem_iInf _).mp ((Submodule.mem_iInf _).mp hv t) ht
    have h₁ : (basis N k).repr ((t : Module.End ℂ (cuspFormsNew N k)) v) g =
        g.heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter t * (basis N k).repr v g :=
      basis_repr_apply_heckeCuspNewRationalAlgebra t v
    rw [h₀, map_zero, Finsupp.zero_apply] at h₁
    exact RingHom.mem_ker.mpr <| (mul_eq_zero.mp h₁.symm).resolve_right hg
  · rintro _ ⟨g, hg, rfl⟩
    refine ⟨basis N k g, (Submodule.mem_iInf _).mpr fun t ↦ (Submodule.mem_iInf _).mpr fun ht ↦ ?_,
      coe_basis_apply g⟩
    rw [LinearMap.mem_ker, apply_basis_eq_heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter_smul,
      RingHom.mem_ker.mp ((isGaloisConjugate_iff_ker_heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter_le hk).mp hg ht),
      zero_smul]

variable (f σ) in
/-- **Galois conjugates of newforms are newforms, if the rational Hecke algebra is a `ℚ`-form**
(LeanBridge issue #38): if the natural map `ℂ ⊗_ℚ T_ℚ → End_ℂ(S_k(Γ₁(N))ⁿᵉʷ)` is injective, then for
every newform `f` of level `N` and weight `k` and every automorphism `σ` of `ℂ`, the Galois
conjugate `σ(f)` is a newform of level `N` and weight `k`. The character `σ ∘ λ_f` of `T_ℚ` extends
to a character of `ℂ ⊗_ℚ T_ℚ`, which is the complex newspace Hecke algebra, hence is the character
of a newform `g`; then `a_p(g) = σ(a_p(f))` at every prime `p`, the nebentypus of `g` is `σ ∘ χ`,
and the Hecke recurrence gives `aₙ(g) = σ(aₙ(f))` for all `n`. -/
lemma exists_isGaloisConjugateBy_of_hasRationalHeckeForm (hH : HasRationalHeckeForm N k) :
    ∃ g : Newform N k, f.IsGaloisConjugateBy σ g := by
  let e : ℂ ⊗[ℚ] heckeCuspNewRationalAlgebra N k ≃ₐ[ℂ] heckeTDiamondCuspNewAlgebra N k :=
    (AlgEquiv.ofInjective _ hH).trans (Subalgebra.equivOfEq _ _ range_heckeCuspNewComplexify)
  let ψ : heckeTDiamondCuspNewAlgebra N k →ₐ[ℂ] ℂ :=
    (lift (ofId ℂ ℂ) ((σ : ℂ →ₐ[ℚ] ℂ).comp f.heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter)
      fun _ _ ↦ Commute.all _ _).comp e.symm.toAlgHom
  rcases Newform.heckeTDiamondCuspNewCharacter_surjective ψ with ⟨g, hg⟩
  have key (t : heckeCuspNewRationalAlgebra N k) :
      g.heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter t = σ (f.heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter t) := by
    have he : e (1 ⊗ₜ t) = ⟨t, heckeCuspNewRationalAlgebra_le t.2⟩ :=
      Subtype.ext <| (AlgEquiv.ofInjective_apply _ hH _).trans <|
        (heckeCuspNewComplexify_tmul 1 t).trans (one_smul ℂ _)
    rw [heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter_apply, hg, ← he]
    simp [ψ]
  exact ⟨g, isGaloisConjugateBy_of_heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter_eq key⟩

lemma hasRationalHeckeForm_of_forall_exists_isGaloisConjugateBy (hk : 2 ≤ k)
    (hS : ∀ (f : Newform N k) (σ : Gal(ℂ/ℚ)), ∃ g : Newform N k, f.IsGaloisConjugateBy σ g) :
    HasRationalHeckeForm N k := by
  classical
  have : Fintype (Newform N k) := Fintype.ofFinite _
  have : Fintype (NewformOrbit N k) := Fintype.ofFinite _
  have : ∀ O : NewformOrbit N k, NumberField (CoefficientField O.out) :=
    fun O ↦ numberField_CoefficientField _ hk
  let Λ : heckeCuspNewRationalAlgebra N k →ₗ[ℚ] ∀ O : NewformOrbit N k, CoefficientField O.out :=
    LinearMap.pi fun O ↦
      { toFun t := ⟨O.out.heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter t,
          heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter_mem_coefficientField t⟩
        map_add' t t' := Subtype.ext (map_add _ t t')
        map_smul' c t := Subtype.ext (map_smul O.out.heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter c t) }
  have hΛ : Function.Injective Λ := fun t t' htt' ↦ Subtype.ext <| (basis N k).ext fun g ↦ by
    have hO : (⟦g⟧ : NewformOrbit N k).out.heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter t =
        (⟦g⟧ : NewformOrbit N k).out.heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter t' :=
      congrArg Subtype.val (congrFun htt' ⟦g⟧)
    rcases Quotient.mk_out (s := galoisOrbitRel N k) g with ⟨σ, hσ⟩
    rw [apply_basis_eq_heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter_smul,
      apply_basis_eq_heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter_smul, hσ.heckeCuspNewRationalCharacter_eq,
      AlgHom.comp_apply, AlgHom.comp_apply, hO]
  have : FiniteDimensional ℚ (heckeCuspNewRationalAlgebra N k) := .of_injective Λ hΛ
  have h₁ : Module.finrank ℚ (heckeCuspNewRationalAlgebra N k) ≤
      ∑ O : NewformOrbit N k, Module.finrank ℚ (CoefficientField O.out) :=
    (LinearMap.finrank_le_finrank_of_injective hΛ).trans_eq (Module.finrank_pi_fintype ℚ)
  have hO (O : NewformOrbit N k) : Module.finrank ℚ (CoefficientField O.out) =
      (Finset.univ.filter fun g : Newform N k ↦ (⟦g⟧ : NewformOrbit N k) = O).card := by
    rw [← ncard_galoisOrbit_eq hk (hS O.out), ← Set.ncard_coe_finset]
    congr 1
    ext g
    simp only [Finset.coe_filter, Finset.mem_univ, true_and]
    exact ⟨fun h ↦ (Quotient.sound h).symm.trans O.out_eq,
      fun h ↦ Quotient.exact (O.out_eq.trans h.symm)⟩
  have h₂ : ∑ O : NewformOrbit N k, Module.finrank ℚ (CoefficientField O.out) =
      Fintype.card (Newform N k) := by
    rw [Finset.sum_congr rfl fun O _ ↦ hO O, ← Finset.card_eq_sum_card_fiberwise
      fun _ _ ↦ Finset.mem_coe.mpr (Finset.mem_univ _), Finset.card_univ]
  have h₃ : Module.finrank ℂ (LinearMap.range (heckeCuspNewComplexify N k).toLinearMap) =
      Fintype.card (Newform N k) := by
    have e : LinearMap.range (heckeCuspNewComplexify N k).toLinearMap =
        Subalgebra.toSubmodule (heckeTDiamondCuspNewAlgebra N k) := by
      rw [← range_heckeCuspNewComplexify]
      rfl
    rw [e, Subalgebra.finrank_toSubmodule,
      Newform.heckeTDiamondCuspNewAlgebraEquiv.toLinearEquiv.finrank_eq,
      Module.finrank_fintype_fun_eq_card]
  have h₄ : Module.finrank ℂ (LinearMap.range (heckeCuspNewComplexify N k).toLinearMap) +
      Module.finrank ℂ (LinearMap.ker (heckeCuspNewComplexify N k).toLinearMap) =
        Module.finrank ℂ (ℂ ⊗[ℚ] heckeCuspNewRationalAlgebra N k) :=
    LinearMap.finrank_range_add_finrank_ker _
  have : Module.Free ℚ (heckeCuspNewRationalAlgebra N k) :=
    @Free.of_divisionRing ℚ _ _ (addCommMonoidToAddCommGroup ℚ) _
  have h₅ : Module.finrank ℂ (ℂ ⊗[ℚ] heckeCuspNewRationalAlgebra N k) =
      Module.finrank ℚ (heckeCuspNewRationalAlgebra N k) :=
    Module.finrank_baseChange
  have h₆ : Module.finrank ℂ (LinearMap.ker (heckeCuspNewComplexify N k).toLinearMap) = 0 := by
    omega
  exact LinearMap.ker_eq_bot.mp <| Submodule.finrank_eq_zero.mp h₆

/-- **The rational Hecke algebra is a `ℚ`-form exactly when all Galois conjugates of newforms are
newforms**: in weight at least two, the hypothesis `TauCeti.HasRationalHeckeForm N k` holds if and
only if, for every newform `f` of level `N` and weight `k` and every automorphism `σ` of `ℂ`, the
Galois conjugate `σ(f)` is a newform (LeanBridge issue #38). If all the `σ(f)` are newforms, the
characters of the newforms embed `T_ℚ` into the product of the coefficient fields of the Galois
orbits, of total degree the number of newforms, which is the dimension of the complex span of
`T_ℚ`. -/
lemma hasRationalHeckeForm_iff (hk : 2 ≤ k) : HasRationalHeckeForm N k ↔
    ∀ (f : Newform N k) (σ : Gal(ℂ/ℚ)), ∃ g : Newform N k, f.IsGaloisConjugateBy σ g :=
  ⟨fun hH f σ ↦ exists_isGaloisConjugateBy_of_hasRationalHeckeForm f σ hH,
    hasRationalHeckeForm_of_forall_exists_isGaloisConjugateBy hk⟩

variable (f σ) in
/-- The **Galois conjugate** `σ(f)` of a newform `f` by an automorphism `σ` of `ℂ`, as a newform of
the same level and weight (LMFDB `cmf.newspaces`, `cmf.galois_conjugate`), if the rational Hecke
algebra is a `ℚ`-form: the newform with coefficients `σ(aₙ)`, which is unique. -/
noncomputable def galoisConj (hH : HasRationalHeckeForm N k) : Newform N k :=
  (exists_isGaloisConjugateBy_of_hasRationalHeckeForm f σ hH).choose

variable (f σ) in
lemma isGaloisConjugateBy_galoisConj (hH : HasRationalHeckeForm N k) :
    f.IsGaloisConjugateBy σ (f.galoisConj σ hH) :=
  (exists_isGaloisConjugateBy_of_hasRationalHeckeForm f σ hH).choose_spec

variable (f) in
lemma galoisConj_one (hH : HasRationalHeckeForm N k) : f.galoisConj 1 hH = f :=
  (f.isGaloisConjugateBy_galoisConj 1 hH).unique f.isGaloisConjugateBy_one

variable (f σ τ) in
/-- **The Galois group acts on newforms** (LMFDB `cmf.newspaces`), through its action on the
coefficients of their `q`-expansions, if the rational Hecke algebra is a `ℚ`-form:
`(στ)(f) = σ(τ(f))`. -/
lemma galoisConj_mul (hH : HasRationalHeckeForm N k) :
    f.galoisConj (σ * τ) hH = (f.galoisConj τ hH).galoisConj σ hH :=
  (f.isGaloisConjugateBy_galoisConj (σ * τ) hH).unique <|
    (f.isGaloisConjugateBy_galoisConj τ hH).trans
      ((f.galoisConj τ hH).isGaloisConjugateBy_galoisConj σ hH)

/-- **The orbits of the Galois action on newforms are the Galois orbits**, if the rational Hecke
algebra is a `ℚ`-form (LMFDB `cmf.newspaces`, `cmf.galois_orbit`). -/
lemma exists_galoisConj_eq_iff (hH : HasRationalHeckeForm N k) :
    (∃ σ, f.galoisConj σ hH = g) ↔ g ∈ f.galoisOrbit :=
  ⟨fun ⟨σ, hσ⟩ ↦ ⟨σ, hσ ▸ f.isGaloisConjugateBy_galoisConj σ hH⟩,
    fun ⟨σ, hσ⟩ ↦ ⟨σ, (f.isGaloisConjugateBy_galoisConj σ hH).unique hσ⟩⟩

/-- **Every embedding of the coefficient field gives a newform, if the rational Hecke algebra is
a `ℚ`-form**: for every embedding `ι : ℚ(f) → ℂ` of the coefficient field of a newform `f`, the
embedding `ι(f) = ∑ ι(aₙ) qⁿ` (LMFDB `cmf.embedding`) is a newform of the level and weight of
`f`. -/
lemma exists_isEmbedding_of_hasRationalHeckeForm (hH : HasRationalHeckeForm N k)
    (ι : CoefficientField f →ₐ[ℚ] ℂ) : ∃ g : Newform N k, f.IsEmbedding g ι :=
  (galoisOrbitEmbedding_surjective (exists_isGaloisConjugateBy_of_hasRationalHeckeForm f · hH)
    ι).elim fun x hx ↦ ⟨x, hx ▸ isEmbedding_galoisOrbitEmbedding x⟩

variable (f) in
/-- **The dimension of a newform is the degree of its coefficient field, if the rational Hecke
algebra is a `ℚ`-form**: in weight at least two, the newform subspace of `f`, the piece of the
newspace spanned by the Galois orbit of `f` (LMFDB `cmf.decomposition.new.gamma0chi`), has
dimension `[ℚ(f) : ℚ]`. -/
lemma dimension_eq_finrank_of_hasRationalHeckeForm (hk : 2 ≤ k) (hH : HasRationalHeckeForm N k) :
    f.dimension = Module.finrank ℚ (CoefficientField f) :=
  dimension_eq_finrank hk fun σ ↦ exists_isGaloisConjugateBy_of_hasRationalHeckeForm f σ hH

variable (σ) in
lemma galoisConj_injective (hH : HasRationalHeckeForm N k) :
    Function.Injective (galoisConj · σ hH) := by
  intro f f' h
  rw [← galoisConj_one f hH, ← galoisConj_one f' hH, ← inv_mul_cancel σ, galoisConj_mul,
    galoisConj_mul]
  exact congrArg (galoisConj · σ⁻¹ hH) h

variable (σ) in
/-- **The spaces of newforms of Galois conjugate characters are Galois conjugate, if the rational
Hecke algebra is a `ℚ`-form**: `σ` maps the newforms of nebentypus `χ` onto those of nebentypus
`σ ∘ χ`, so that it maps a basis of `S_k^{new}(N, χ)` onto one of `S_k^{new}(N, σ ∘ χ)`
(LMFDB `cmf.decomposition.new.gamma1`). -/
lemma image_galoisConj_setOf_χ_eq (hH : HasRationalHeckeForm N k) :
    (galoisConj · σ hH) '' {f | f.χ = χ} = {g | g.χ = (Units.map (σ : ℂ →* ℂ)).comp χ} := by
  refine Set.ext fun g ↦ ⟨?_, fun hg ↦ ⟨g.galoisConj σ⁻¹ hH, ?_, ?_⟩⟩
  · rintro ⟨f, hf, rfl⟩
    exact (f.isGaloisConjugateBy_galoisConj σ hH).χ_eq.trans
      (congrArg (Units.map (σ : ℂ →* ℂ)).comp hf)
  · refine (g.isGaloisConjugateBy_galoisConj σ⁻¹ hH).χ_eq.trans ?_
    rw [Set.mem_ofPred_eq.mp hg]
    ext u
    simp
  · exact (galoisConj_mul g σ σ⁻¹ hH).symm.trans <| by rw [mul_inv_cancel, galoisConj_one]

variable (σ) in
/-- **Galois conjugate characters have spaces of newforms of the same dimension, if the rational
Hecke algebra is a `ℚ`-form**: `S_k^{new}(N, σ ∘ χ)` and `S_k^{new}(N, χ)` have the same dimension
(LMFDB `cmf.decomposition.new.gamma1`). -/
lemma finrank_cuspFormsNew_inf_cuspFormCharSpace_comp_of_hasRationalHeckeForm
    (hH : HasRationalHeckeForm N k) :
    Module.finrank ℂ ↥(cuspFormsNew N k ⊓ cuspFormCharSpace k ((Units.map (σ : ℂ →* ℂ)).comp χ)) =
      Module.finrank ℂ ↥(cuspFormsNew N k ⊓ cuspFormCharSpace k χ) := by
  rw [← span_image_toCuspForm_eq_cuspFormsNew_inf_cuspFormCharSpace,
    ← span_image_toCuspForm_eq_cuspFormsNew_inf_cuspFormCharSpace, finrank_span_image_toCuspForm,
    finrank_span_image_toCuspForm, ← image_galoisConj_setOf_χ_eq σ χ hH,
    Set.ncard_image_of_injective _ (galoisConj_injective σ hH)]

/-- **The trace bound exists, if the rational Hecke algebra is a `ℚ`-form**: in weight at least
two, the traces of the first `m` coefficients distinguish the Galois orbits of newforms of
nebentypus `χ` for some `m ≥ 1`, so that the trace bound (LMFDB `cmf.trace_bound`) is the least
such `m`, and not the junk value `0`. -/
lemma exists_tracesDistinguishNewforms_of_hasRationalHeckeForm (hk : 2 ≤ k)
    (hH : HasRationalHeckeForm N k) : ∃ m, 0 < m ∧ TracesDistinguishNewforms N k χ m :=
  exists_tracesDistinguishNewforms hk
    (fun f σ ↦ exists_isGaloisConjugateBy_of_hasRationalHeckeForm f σ hH) χ

end HeckeRing.GL2.Newform
